rting with ${x}_{0}=0.1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{{x}_{0}(\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{0}+1)}{{x}_{0}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.1\\,(\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.1)+1)}{0.1-1} \\\\  & =0.144…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}(\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{1}+1)}{{x}_{1}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.144…(\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.144…)+1)}{0.144⋯-1} \\\\  & =0.157…, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{{x}_{2}(\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}_{2}+1)}{{x}_{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.157…(\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0.157…)+1)}{0.157⋯-1} \\\\  & =0.158….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{2}≈0.16$ and ${x}_{3}≈0.16$ are the same when rounded to two decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x≈0.16,$ rounded to two decimal places." 13194139535128 true] [17592186332670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332671 13194139535128 true] [17592186332670 1000 #edb/ref 17592186332672 13194139535128 true] [17592186332670 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535128 true] [17592186332670 1041 "field-1" 13194139535128 true] [17592186332670 1104 #edb/ref 17592186332672 13194139535128 true] [17592186332670 1110 #uuid "eaa8fe1e-e01e-5701-be64-85ec7cf062fd" 13194139535128 true] [17592186332671 1034 "0.14" 13194139535128 true] [17592186332671 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535128 true] [17592186332671 1111 #uuid "3c83b555-37b0-5aff-b860-4d016d058146" 13194139535128 true] [17592186332672 1034 "0.16" 13194139535128 true] [17592186332672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535128 true] [17592186332672 1111 #uuid "93ecca60-c5fb-54b5-8c1d-2a4f96b41f07" 13194139535128 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-255772/field-1/7843a997f76850e5a62cfb625d96d402e51a5570468db204bdea068d973efe17" 17592186332623 "q-255772/field-1/7e5fca3b3a327f0883354c585138a3286513bf87d6433c64cf8b726aa7dbedf1" 17592186332624 "q-255772/field-2/3f60266fcdbd7728b865f97203dcbcfd8bc6bc8518df9e2803ba4efc27775587" 17592186332625 "q-255853/field-1/2468d3f08d897d95f4d28b48c13e